1. Identify the merge conflict: After pushing your branch to GitHub and attempting to merge another branch into it, you may encounter a merge conflict. You'll see a message indicating that there were merge conflicts that need to be resolved, and the merge will be blocked until you do so. To find this message, look for a red exclamation mark or an "! " (exclamation point) next to your repository name in the header of your GitHub page, or in the "Pull Request" or "Merge Request" tab if you're using those features. Click on it to see more information about the merge conflict.

